🐛 Describe the bug
Hello. I am using a c++ version of pytorch. I have the follow code
auto opts1 = torch::TensorOptions().dtype(torch::kInt);
auto opts2 = torch::TensorOptions().dtype(torch::kFloat);
torch::Tensor t1 = torch::zeros({3,3},opts2);
torch::Tensor i = torch::tensor({0,1,1,2},opts1);
torch::Tensor j = torch::tensor({1,1,1,1},opts1);
std::cout << "t1\n" << t1<<std::endl;
t1.index_put_({i,j},torch::tensor({1,2,3,4},opts2),true); //Error here
std::cout << "t1\n" << t1 <<std::endl;
When i use in-place operation of "index_put_", i get some error. I don't understand the error because i work in CLion with CMake and use MSVC compiler. All I see are assembler operations and addresses in disassembled code.
i noticed one thing. If i remove bool argument for accumulating, it'll work. I don't understand why it happens.
